g in plain  sight but the solution when all the  fighting is over and both Michael and  Corey are dead isn't to keep hiding or  to lock herself away in Haddonfield like  her grandmother once did instead Alison  leaves her hometown behind to start  fresh somewhere else while she seems  hopeful it's clear that Alison is all  too aware of the true evils of the world  and well equipped to take care of  herself  following the losses at the end of  Halloween kills the pool of Michael  Myers survivors has shrunk considerably  one major player who stuck around for  Halloween ends alongside Lori and  Allison is Lindsay Wallace played by  Kyle Richards of course in 1978's  Halloween Lindsay was Annie brackett's  babysitting charge her babysitter Andy  bracket was executed that night Lindsay  managed to hide from Michael in  Halloween kills and survive four years  later Lindsay seems to have a pretty  good life she's running a local bar  throwing festive Halloween parties for  the locals and even growing closer to  Lori and Ellison but when violence  starts to creep back into Haddonfield  Lindsay is swept up in the Michael Myers  stereo once again however Richard's  character doesn't play as big a part in  Halloween ends and she doesn't face the  same level of violence that follows  Laurie and Allison by the end of the  film Lindsay stands as one of only a  handful of survivors of the original  1978 Massacre alongside Lori as far as  we can tell it seems like she'll remain  in Haddonfield field where she'll be an  important part of the town's future  particularly since she knows how to move  on from tragedy will Patton's Deputy  Frank Hawkins was one of the men who  arrested Michael Myers on Halloween  night in 1978. in Halloween kills we  learned that Frank and Lori once had a  strong flirtation that could have turned  into something more if they weren't both  so damaged and reluctant I always liked  you in Halloween ends Frank and Lori run  into each other in a grocery store and  it seems like it might finally be the  right time to pick up where they left  off at the end of the film following  Lori's gruesome battle with Michael  Myers Frank stops by Lori's House the  pairs sit together on her front steps  and it suggested that Laurie might  finally be ready to take a chance on  romance now that her boogeyman is behind  her while it's unclear whether or not  they'll actually get together viewers  are left with a sense of hope for a  potential shared future  Halloween ends is based around the story  of Corey Cunningham a local Haddonfield  kid whose world was shattered on  Halloween night in 2019. Corey was  responsible for the death of a child he  was babysitting making him a town Pariah  and leaving him with a lifetime of Lost  Dreams however Corey's guilt is  eventually eclipsed by his desire to  understand his own darkness and go  deeper into it something he's able to do  when he crosses paths with Michael Myers  in a sewer Dream by the end of the film  Corey has essentially proclaimed himself  the new Haddonfield Boogeyman he even  goes so far as to steal and wear  Michael's mask in an attempt to get  revenge on all the people who have  wronged him of course Lori is smarter  than Corey and manages to stop him in  his tracks after leaving a path of  bodies in his wake Corey becomes  integral to haddonfield's tragic Legacy  but for now at least it's unclear  whether he is a new Boogeyman or just a  footnote in the story of Michael Myers  Haddonfield is a town that has been  rocked by an absurd amount of tragedy  over the course of 40 years and it's  taken a toll even with Michael Myers  gone the town continues to suffer what  feels like an ongoing series of  accidents deaths suicide and other  tragedies there's a darkness in  Haddonfield which Lori Witnesses even  when she does something as benign as  going to the grocery store it's also  revealed that some of Michael's  survivors and their families blame her  for provoking the killer to more  violence Michael's death at the end of  the film and the ceremonial crushing of  his body at the junkyard temporarily  puts an end to this Darkness but viewers  are left with more questions about the  future of Haddonfield such as will the  town ever truly be free of the Specter  of evil will more people like Corey  Cunningham rise up to take Michael's  place or as haddenfield finally able to  live in a world of Safety and Security  once again it's an understatement to say  that the town's been through a lot and  the road to any sort of recovery is  bound to be very long  though Michael has seemingly died in  other Halloween films none of them quite  matched the death he was given in  Halloween ends after being pinned to a  table by Lori and Allison Michael was  bled to death through several cuts to  key arteries along his body but as  Allison astutely noted Michael Myers  still wasn't quite dead enough with the  support of local law enforcement and  much of the Town Lori and Allison took  Michael's body to the nearby junkyard  there they placed him in a grinder and  crushed him to pieces while his body has  destroyed everyone is left wondering  whether Michael Myers can ever really be  killed in Halloween kills Lori theorized  that Michael Myers seemed to possess a  superhuman ability when it came to  killing and cheating death the more he  kills the more he transcends into  something else Halloween ends seemingly  demonstrates Lori's theory in one  particular scene Michael kills Allison's  ex-boyfriend and his body seems to  almost immediately recover some of its  strengths but were never told where  Michael's immense strength comes from or  whether someone else can actually access  it while Corey seems to believe that he  can take over from Michael and perhaps  acquire some of that power his fast  demise suggests otherwise Michael Myers  is dead the ending of Halloween ends  makes that clear by showing us his  corpse then crushing that corpse in a  brutal piece of junkyard Machinery the  film is intent on making sure that this  Michael Myers timeline is complete and  that Lori strode's fighting Days Are  Over except not all of Michael is really  gone at least not the version of Michael  that emerged when he pulled on his mask  and became the shape the final shot of  the film reveals that the mask battered  and burned is still present in Lori's  house as a dark souvenir of her Victory  Lori probably wanted to keep the  horrifying object because she didn't  want collectors or copycats to get their  hands on it it's also worth noting that  she could have destroyed the mask but  she didn't Lori's decision to save the a  mask raises a number of intriguing  questions for one we're left wondering  if the mask might hold power over Lori  now that it's in her possession Michael  never wanted to remove the mask and he  would stop whatever he was doing to pull  it back down if someone tried to take it  from him plus Michael's apparent  Transcendent abilities while wearing the  mask suggests that it's more than just a  face covering if so Lori may have made a  terrible mistake in keeping the mask as  a trophy Haddonfield is a relatively  small town that's been rocked by some  serious tragedies Through The Years in  fact Corey Cunningham is the second  major mass murderer to come out of the  town in 40 years and his Killing Spree  is inextricably linked to the  devastation caused by Michael Myers in  2018's Halloween a pair of True Crime  podcasters came to town with a specific  focus on the town's 1978 tragedy proving  that there was widespread interest in  the case and in Halloween ends Lori  Strode completes her Memoir about  Michael Myers and it seems likely that  the book will throw Haddonfield into the  national Spotlight once again as  haddenfield looks to a future without  the serial killer will Lori Embark upon  a book tour to promote her work will the  town's various True Crime stops become  tourist destinations basically following  Corey's murder spree and the death of  Michael Myers haddonfield's profile is  on the rise even if the trilogy has come  to an end  Halloween ends represents an interesting  Benchmark in the history of the  Halloween franchise it's not the first  film that has attempted to kill off  Michael Myers for instance Michael and  Dr Sam Loomis were blown to Smithereens  in 1981's Halloween 2 and they both  managed to return in the fourth film in  1998 Lori decapitated Michael with a  fire ax in Halloween H2O however this  version of events was retconned in  2002's follow-up Halloween resurrection  Michael's deaths didn't seem as final  and definitive in those earlier films as  the one in Halloween ends but may he  never  have a rest in peace whether Michael's  dead or not fans clearly still have an  appetite for the Halloween series but as  for where the franchise might go next is  currently unclear while Jamie Lee Curtis  seems to be well and truly done with  playing Lori Strode there's a  possibility that the series could be  rebooted in the future by a different  Studio blumhouse no longer has the  rights to the franchise having agreed to  deliver only three films but producer  Jason Blum and original Creator John  Carpenter have both suggested that as  long as Halloween films make money  someone will want to make more of them  Halloween could also live on without  Michael 1982's Halloween 3 season of The  Witch which doesn't feature the serial  killer has developed a cult following in  the years since its release in fact some  fans have even wondered if new films in  the franchise could actually revisit the  Season of the Witch timeline or take  some other radically new approach  regardless of what happens next it's  clear that the Halloween franchise is  never really over as Michael buyers  always comes back

